# .dockerignore — keep the build context small and free of host state.
#
# This matters more than usual for this repo: without it, `docker build` ships
# the developer's 1GB+ backend/.venv, a populated node_modules, and the live
# agent memory stores (which contain real investigation data) into the daemon
# and into every intermediate layer. The stores in particular must never end up
# baked into a published image.

# ── Version control ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.git
.gitignore
.github/CONTRIBUTING.md

# ── Secrets ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# .env is loaded by the app at runtime, never baked into an image. Shipping it
# would put every API key in a layer anyone with the image can read.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# ── Python ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# The venv is host-specific (absolute paths, platform-specific binaries) and is
# rebuilt inside the image. Including it breaks the build and leaks local state.
**/.venv
**/venv
**/__pycache__
**/*.pyc
**/*.pyo
**/*.pyd
**/*.egg-info
**/.pytest_cache
**/.mypy_cache
**/.ruff_cache
**/*.so
backend/.venv

# ── Node ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
**/node_modules
**/.next
**/out
**/turbo
**/.turbo
**/tsconfig.tsbuildinfo
**/.eslintcache
.npm

# ── Agent runtime state: real investigation data, never image content ───────
backend/vault_store
backend/sentinel_store
backend/reports
vault_store
sentinel_store
reports

# ── Local dev artefacts ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────
**/*.log
logs
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
.idea
.vscode
*.swp
.pytest_cache
.ruff_cache
coverage
.coverage
coverage.xml
htmlcov

# ── Build/test output ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────
dist
build
out
target

# ── Docs and agent context ──────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Kept out of the runtime image; the deployed container serves the app, not the
# repo's internal documentation.
graphify-out
docs
*.md
!README.md
CLAUDE.md
AGENTS.md
LICENSE

# ── Deployment config not needed at runtime ─────────────────────────────────
# The image is built FROM these; keeping them in context only slows the build.
vercel.json
railway.json
.dockerignore
.dockerignore-frontend
Makefile
docker-compose.yml
docker-compose.override.yml
docker-compose.override.yml.example

# ── VCS / CI metadata ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.github/workflows
.github/ISSUE_TEMPLATE

# ── Keep ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Explicitly retained (the patterns above are all additive exclusions, so this
# is belt-and-braces documentation rather than an override):
#   backend/**/*.py       — the application
#   backend/requirements.txt
#   frontend/{app,components,lib,public}/**  — the dashboard
#   frontend/package.json, package-lock.json
#   infra/supervisord.conf
